eline_reference.py, diagnose an observed limitation, check primary nearest work, and implement a feasible candidate. Write proposal.json containing study (matching study_schema), parent_trial (existing trial ID), and variants (1-4 objects with distinct name, file basename ending .py, role candidate/control, config object, and note). At least one candidate is required. Add key ablations or matched controls for the claimed mechanism when feasible; reference existing matched trials as controls where justified. Each variant is a standalone module. Do not run training. New architecture choices come from evidence; industry cards do not mandate them.\"\ncandidate_api {\"Model\": \"Model(feature_map, model_id=..., gpu=0, **kwargs) -> torch.nn.Module; optional MultiTaskModel utilities. forward(inputs) returns {label+\\\"_pred\\\": probability [B,1]} for all four tasks. Host places the module on the assigned GPU.\", \"architecture_scope\": \"Whole-model design for unified modeling. Model need not inherit the initial reference, retain its pooling, or use separate task towers; representations, interactions, routing and readout can all be replaced.\", \"lineage\": \"parent_trial records the empirical comparison and evidence lineage. A complete rewrite may have no inherited architectural components.\", \"proposal_unit\": \"Coordinated structural changes implementing one coherent mechanism are allowed; isolate their effects through planned replacement, component or factorial controls.\", \"meta\": \"Read-only UniRank FeatureMap: features (ordered specs, sources, vocab_size), labels, data_dir. Full framework reference files are available through tools.py.\", \"batch\": [\"inputs=(batch_dict,item_dict,history_mask,multi_task_history_masks)\", \"batch_dict: categorical user/context features int64[B]; current labels and lookup metadata are removed by host\", \"item_dict: item_id,cate_id,campaign_id,customer_id,brand,price_bucket,action, each int64[B,101]; last position is current target, preceding100 are pre-padded history\", \"history_mask: float 0/1 [B,100]; four task masks: [B,100]; use only masked history\", \"Target action is always zero (unknown/padding), never a current label. Historical feedback policy is frozen in protocol.history_policy.\", \"Historical item_id is a previous advertisement ID. Shopping events used to create auxiliary labels are only matched by user/category/brand.\", \"No raw timestamps, event-time deltas, raw user IDs, full future histories, current labels or global sample indexes are supplied to forward.\"], \"task_labels\": [\"is_click\", \"cart\", \"fav\", \"buy\"], \"primary\": \"Validation macro AUC = (is_click AUC + cart AUC + fav AUC + buy AUC)/4. Checkpoint, incumbent, topic gains and final selection all use this rule. Exact ties prefer lower mean Logloss, then fewer parameters, then trial ID. Report every task change; explain trade-offs.\", \"optional\": [\"Literal CONFIG dict for model architecture only; all frozen host parameters are rejected.\", \"Model.training_loss(inputs, probabilities[B,4], train_labels[B,4]) -> finite differentiable scalar; labels supplied only during training. Default is sum of four unweighted BCEs.\"], \"ownership\": \"Edit candidate modules/proposal only. No filesystem/network operations in model source. Imports: torch,numpy,math,typing,copy,functools,collections,itertools,dataclasses,contextlib,unirank,model_zoo. Host owns training, input filtering and scoring.\", \"local_checks\": \"Coding jail has no torch; check syntax/source there. Host trains and scores. Do not install or train inside coding jail.\", \"training\": \"From scratch; same frozen data, seed, epochs, batch, history limit and dense AdamW / embedding Adagrad. Architecture may be rewritten completely. Retain causal controls and account for added parameters/computation.\"}\nCONTEXT KEYS ['history', 'allowed_observation_ids', 'previous_runtime_error', 'trajectory_index', 'incumbent', 'remaining_seconds', 'protocol', 'met