4 LayerNorm parameters and4*32*32 attention maps; host counts authoritative. Host gates, all charged and pending: finite four[B,1] outputs and finite sum-BCE backward in FP32/BF16, batch8192 peak memory and latency; empty,one,100 and holey histories; perturb masked IDs including out-of-vocabulary values, masked task masks and current target action in eval/cloned train modes. Valid past feedback may affect the inherited g0 path. At paired initialization compare every inherited R12 tensor/buffer and CPU RNG; zero exchange output must replay R12 predictions, Dice updates and original-parameter gradients. The new output weight can have nonzero gradient immediately because memory includes shared DIN content and learned identities. Upstream exchange parameters receive zero gradient at zero output by design; use a cloned nonzero-output diagnostic to require live projection/query/key/value/identity gradients. Verify mean-source attention remains active/query-dependent with distinct identities on a nondegenerate fixture. Isolate the exchange for mean-preserving summary perturbations: mean source invariant, private source can change; direct private towers can respond in both full models. Empty-history exchange update must remain exactly zero even with nonzero diagnostic weights. Source choice affects only new memory, never task_routing. Record macro and every task AUC/Logloss, deltas versus DIN/g0/g3/R12, cost versus both R12 and mean control, parameters, train/inference/full wall, latency and peak GPU memory. Retain every failed receipt; candidate_diagnostics in historical runs are not_requested, so old notes do not prove these gates passed. Host-supported history bins use existing boundaries0,1-16,17-64,>64 with samples and positive/negative counts; other unavailable slices/bootstrap inputs are not invented. No test access. No writable separate scientific-memory API is exposed; this prospective evidence-linked proposal preserves local observations without editing read-only 