, and auxiliary labels match user/category/brand rather than advertisement conversions. Conclusions remain offline benchmark-specific.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n {'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':'task_exchange_private: add four private task-summary memory slots read by existing tokens before JointBlock','control':'task_exchange_mean: same module, IDs, parameters, operator shapes and private direct tower summaries; replace only new memory source with repeated mean S','held_fixed':fixed,'remaining_confounds':['effective representational subspace differs intentionally','new gradients into existing task scorers differ','one fixed seed; training cost must be measured'],'decision_if_supported':'Treat private-minus-mean as local controlled evidence for distinct-summary utility at this location only if private also exceeds R12; reserve paired repetition before a stronger claim.','decision_if_not_supported':'Reject a task-specificity interpretation for this implementation. If both improve similarly, attribute provisionally to a common-summary exchange/capacity path; otherwise retain R12.'},\n {'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':'Both proposed exchange variants relative to archived unchanged R12','control':'g3-r0012-memory_task_private_linear, independently source-identical at entry; g3-r0014-scorer_grad_open is same-seed replay, not another seed','held_fixed':fixed[:6],'remaining_confounds':['+7936 dense parameters and extra attention operators','earlier task pool evaluation order','historical versus new runtime noise; no equal-compute training claim'],'decision_if_supported':'Compare mean control and actual cost before adopting. Freeze selected source/config/checkpoint and closest control suite for validation-only repetitions.','decision_if_not_supported':'Keep committed R12 as best supported integration. Do not turn a new-path failure into rejection of R12 or all task conditioning.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed','intervention':'Report new variants and incumbent against both frozen sources and initial DIN','control':'g0-r0011-memory_joint_collapsed; g3-r0010-content_plus_linear_private; baseline-din; existing R12 private/mean x linear/copy factorial','held_fixed':fixed[:4],'remaining_confounds':['architectural and parameter differences; these are performance references, not a new complete integration factorial','source controls and current best lack paired independent seeds'],'decision_if_supported':'Report macro/per-task AUC and Logloss deltas and measured quality/cost separately; existing single-seed factorial remains provisional attribution.','decision_if_not_supported':'Report regressions faithfully; beating a source without beating R12 is not new progress.'}\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g3-r0012-memory_task_private_linear:594.1056 wall/541.7392 train/43.0575 validation-inference seconds; R15 private64:682.3146 wall and shared210:650.9998 wall. Runtime estimated unit483.4166s and trial cap1208.5414s; cap is not an estimate or an additional allowance. Snapshot remaining4785.2869s; preparations consume it. Budget430? No: the unchanged campaign hard budget is43200s, deadline1794241824.5008233. Allocate conservatively 650-700s per proposed full run, 1300-1400s total plus charged gates; measure actual cost.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'One of the two full runs (~700s) is reserved for the active mean-source control and is included, not added again, in the 1400s screen allocation. Reuse matching-protocol source receipts and R12 factorial without uncharged replays. Count numerical diagnostics, source checks, failures and any retries in the same campaign. No third exploratory arm, installations or local training.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Reserve about2500s after this two-arm screen for validation-only paired repetitions: two additional seeds of the selected new variant and archived R12 closest control would cost approximately2*(650+594)=2488s, giving three seeds including the screen when feasible. Host must authorize/schedule seeds under its assessment interface; do not encode seed or epochs in architecture CONFIG. This reserve cannot also fund three-seed repetition of every source/control. Freeze selection and suite first; if specificity remains the central claim, include the mean-source control by reducing the achievable seed count explicitly rather than pretending the reserve covers all three models. If new arms lose, prioritize R12 versus g0 repetition within the remaining resources. No holdout is available.',\n 'stop_rule':'Respect the unchanged campaign deadline and1208.5414s per-trial cap. All preparation, diagnostics, failures, screening, controls and assessments count. Before each host job use its current ledger: stop exploration if the estimated next complete unit plus necessary assessment reserve does not fit. After the two submitted variants, freeze or stop; no automatic repeat of an unknown execution state. If costs exceed estimates, report omitted repetitions and keep single-seed conclusions preliminary; never raise caps, change recipe or inspect held-out outputs.'\n}}\n# Remove an editorial intermediate from the estimate; only the fixed budget is operative.\nstudy['cost_plan']['estimate_ref']=study['cost_plan']['estimate_ref'].replace('Budget430? No: the unchanged campaign hard budget is43200s','The unchanged campaign hard budget is43200s')\nnames=['task_exchange_private','task_exchange_mean']\nassessments=[\n {'knowledge_id':'paper:din','decision':'used','rationale':'Read archived primary weighted-sum and non-normalization mechanism at lines255-283; the existing event pooling is retained.','transformed_mechanism':'No new DIN mechanism: normalized attention is confined to four task-summary memory slots.','variant_names':names,'nearest_work_difference':'A local unified-model extension, not exact DIN reproduction.','falsifier':'Any unintended change of the inherited event pooling invalidates preservation.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-infnet','decision':'used','rationale':'Read pinned benchmark aggregation/broadcast implementation and benchmark section2.3 after finding the local late-readout restriction. It is the nearest inspected information-flow analogy, not evidence of transfer or original-paper equivalence.','transformed_mechanism':'One strictly masked summary-to-token attention residual before the existing interaction; replace private summaries by their mean as the active matched control. No repeated multi-view hubs or affine broadcast code copied.','variant_names':names,'nearest_work_difference':'Four learned compressed task summaries inside R12 versus repeated categorical/sequence/task hub aggregation and broadcast. Original-paper novelty remains unverified.','falsifier':'Failure to beat both R12 and the mean-source control opposes added task-specific utility for this implementation.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'paper:infnet','decision':'unresolved','rationale':'Resolved provenance and attempted authorized read; original text is unavailable. Read the explicit benchmark fallback and pinned code, and retain the source-availability limitation.','transformed_mechanism':'No original-paper result or equivalence claim imported.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Only the benchmark implementation was checked; original priority is unverified.','falsifier':'Original-source audit could identify closer overlap; it is needed before a stronger originality claim.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-ultrahstu','decision':'rejected','rationale':'No measured long-sequence transduction or sparse-attention bottleneck motivates replacing the100-event representation in this contrast.','transformed_mechanism':'No mechanism adopted.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'No event transduction, truncation or sparse attention changes.','falsifier':'Reconsider after diagnostics identify a sequence-transduction bottleneck and original-source inspection.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-est','decision':'considered','rationale':'Its feature-specific FFN/cross-attention description is adjacent, but R15 extra scorer capacity did not exceed R12. This study changes summary information flow without adding feature-specific FFNs; original paper was not read.','transformed_mechanism':'No EST-specific mechanism imported.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Four compressed summary slots read by existing tokens rather than a feature-specific repeated interaction stack.','falsifier':'A later controlled test could implicate field-specific transformation instead.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-tokenformer','decision':'rejected','rationale':'Full field/event token exchange changes several components and compute at once; the source card also flags masking concerns. Original paper not read.','transformed_mechanism':'No full-history Flex Attention or TokenFormer code adopted.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Retain compressed incumbent histories; add only four memory slots with explicit key masks.','falsifier':'Reconsider if a controlled compact-summary test establishes lost event-level information.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'paper:tokenformer','decision':'unresolved','rationale':'Search metadata only; no primary original text inspected and no result transferred.','transformed_mechanism':'None.','variant_names':[],'nearest_work_difference':'Exact original-method overlap is unverified.','falsifier':'Primary inspection is required before any future priority or reproduction claim.'}\n]\ncommon_note=('Host reproduction: import the listed standalone module, construct Model(feature_map, **CONFIG), and use the host trainer under protocol '+protocol+'. No host CLI/raw data are exposed here; do not invent a local training command. Executable local source check: python3 -m py_compile candidate.py control_mean_exchange.py. Expected per arm33077193 total/31793216 embedding/1283977 dense parameters (+7936 over R12), from112*32 input map,4*32 identities,2*64 LayerNorm parameters and4*32*32 attention maps; host counts authoritative. Host gates, all charged and pending: finite four[B,1] outputs and finite sum-BCE backward in FP32/BF16, batch8192 peak memory and latency; empty,one,100 and holey histories; perturb masked IDs including out-of-vocabulary values, masked task masks and current target action in eval/cloned train modes. Valid past feedback may affect the inherited g0 path. At paired initialization compare every inherited R12 tensor/buffer and CPU RNG; zero exchange output must replay R12 predictions, Dice updates and original-parameter gradients. The new output weight can have nonzero gradient immediately because memory includes shared DIN content and learned identities. Upstream exchange parameters receive zero gradient at zero output by design; use a cloned nonzero-output diagnostic to require live projection/query/key/value/identity gradients. Verify mean-source attention remains active/query-dependent with distinct identities on a nondegenerate fixture. Isolate the exchange for mean-preserving summary perturbations: mean source invariant, private source can change; direct private towers can respond in both full models. Empty-history exchange update must remain exactly zero even with nonzero diagnostic weights. Source choice affects only new memory, never task_routing. Record macro and every task AUC/Logloss, deltas versus DIN/g0/g3/R12, cost versus both R12 and mean control, parameters, train/inference/full wall, latency and peak GPU memory. Retain every failed receipt; candidate_diagnostics in historical runs are not_requested, so old notes do not prove these gates passed. Host-supported history bins use existing boundaries0,1-16,17-64,>64 with samples and positive/negative counts; other unavailable slices/bootstrap inputs are not invented. No test access. No writable separate scientific-memory API is exposed; this prospective evidence-linked proposal preserves local observations without editing read-only human/host evidence. ')\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,role in [(names[0],'candidate.py','candidate'),(names[1],'control_mean_exchange.py','control')]:\n tree=ast.parse(Path(file).read_text());config=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n variants.append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':config,'note':common_note+'Source SHA256 '+hashlib.sha256(Path(file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()+'.'})\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':parent,'variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':assessments}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with two standalone variants and seven knowledge assessments')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\nWrote proposal.json with two standalone variants and seven knowledge assessments\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
